WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.200
Welcome to Grade 5 English, Unit 1: There’s a Lesson in That.

2
00:00:04.900 --> 00:00:06.060
Welcome to Unit 1!

3
00:00:06.620 --> 00:00:11.740
In this unit, you will explore stories
that teach us important lessons about life.

4
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:18.700
You will read a fable, learn new vocabulary, practise
grammar, and write your own short story with a moral.

5
00:00:19.900 --> 00:00:23.480
Every story has something to teach us — let’s find out what!

6
00:00:23.480 --> 00:00:29.860
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

7
00:00:30.660 --> 00:00:36.940
By the end of this unit, you will be able to read
and understand a fable and identify its moral lesson.

8
00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:43.740
you will also recognise features of fables and folklore,
including animal characters and moral teachings.

9
00:00:44.420 --> 00:00:51.420
you will also use adjectives + prepositions correctly
in sentences (e.g., proud of, anxious about).

10
00:00:52.240 --> 00:00:54.140
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

11
00:00:54.960 --> 00:01:02.640
Your vocabulary work begins with these words:
coal, pouch, encounter, regions, misty, anxiety.

12
00:01:03.560 --> 00:01:08.440
Listen to each pronunciation in the
vocabulary lab, study its meaning in context,

13
00:01:08.920 --> 00:01:11.620
and use the word accurately in
your own discussion and writing.

14
00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:20.600
The reading sequence includes There’s a Lesson in That:
source text 1 and There’s a Lesson in That: source text 2.

15
00:01:21.500 --> 00:01:22.360
Read actively.

16
00:01:22.860 --> 00:01:27.300
Identify each text's central ideas,
notice viewpoint and reliability,

17
00:01:27.860 --> 00:01:31.280
and support every inference with
relevant evidence from the text.

18
00:01:32.340 --> 00:01:37.380
The first language focus is What
Are Adjectives + Prepositions?.

19
00:01:37.880 --> 00:01:41.840
An adjective is a word that describes a noun or a pronoun.

20
00:01:42.520 --> 00:01:45.340
It tells us about a quality, feeling, or characteristic.

21
00:01:45.340 --> 00:01:53.020
For example: proud, anxious, afraid, excited, interested,
good, sorry, angry, kind, grateful, jealous, keen.

22
00:01:53.980 --> 00:01:59.680
A preposition is a small word that shows the relationship
between the adjective and the thing it refers to.

23
00:02:00.520 --> 00:02:07.300
Common prepositions include: of,
about, in, at, for, with, to, on.

24
00:02:08.180 --> 00:02:14.140
Notice the structure in the model examples, then apply
it deliberately in connected sentences and paragraphs.

25
00:02:15.320 --> 00:02:19.380
In speaking, you will complete
Speaking 1: Discussion Questions.

26
00:02:19.960 --> 00:02:24.400
Organise your ideas, use evidence
and respond clearly to questions.

27
00:02:25.140 --> 00:02:27.820
In writing, you will plan, draft, check and revise.

28
00:02:28.560 --> 00:02:31.420
Use the success criteria before submitting your work.

29
00:02:31.980 --> 00:02:33.160
You are ready to begin.

30
00:02:33.760 --> 00:02:39.940
Start with the vocabulary lab, continue through
reading and comprehension, apply the grammar focus,

31
00:02:39.940 --> 00:02:42.760
and complete the speaking and writing practices.

32
00:02:43.790 --> 00:02:49.000
Use AI English for hints and feedback, and
bring your questions to the live sessions.
